.\"
.\" MKDIR(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH MKDIR 2 "January 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
mkdir \- create a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/stat.h>
.PP
.BI "int mkdir(const char *" pathname ", mode_t " mode ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR mkdir ()
attempts to create a directory named
.IR pathname .
.PP
The argument
.I mode
specifies the mode for the new directory, modified by the process's
.BR umask (2).
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned.
.PP
On error, \-1 is returned, and
.I errno
is set appropriately.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EEXIST
.I pathname
already exists.
.TP
.B ENOENT
A directory component in
.I pathname
does not exist.
.TP
.B EACCES
Write permission denied for the parent directory.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 39
Arguments:      pathname, mode (on stack)
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rmdir (2),
.BR stat (2),
.BR substrate (7)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2001, POSIX.1-2008.
